            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53539",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "python-multipart: Python-Multipart: Denial of Service via crafted form-urlencoded bodies"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Python-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Prior to 0.0.30, when parsing application/x-www-form-urlencoded bodies, QuerystringParser located the field separator with a two step lookup: it first scanned the entire remaining buffer for \u0026, and only when no \u0026 existed anywhere ahead did it fall back to scanning for ;. For a body that uses ; as the separator and contains no \u0026, every field iteration performed a full failed \u0026 scan over the entire remaining buffer before locating the nearby ;. With N semicolon separated fields in a chunk of size B, this yields O(B^2) byte comparisons per chunk. An attacker can submit a small crafted body of the form a;a;a;... and cause the parser to spend seconds of CPU per request. A handful of concurrent requests can exhaust worker processes. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.0.30."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53539",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53539\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: python-multipart\nFixed Version: 0.0.30\nLink: [CVE-2026-53539](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53539)\nPython-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Prior to 0.0.30, when parsing application/x-www-form-urlencoded bodies, QuerystringParser located the field separator with a two step lookup: it first scanned the entire remaining buffer for \u0026, and only when no \u0026 existed anywhere ahead did it fall back to scanning for ;. For a body that uses ; as the separator and contains no \u0026, every field iteration performed a full failed \u0026 scan over the entire remaining buffer before locating the nearby ;. With N semicolon separated fields in a chunk of size B, this yields O(B^2) byte comparisons per chunk. An attacker can submit a small crafted body of the form a;a;a;... and cause the parser to spend seconds of CPU per request. A handful of concurrent requests can exhaust worker processes. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.0.30.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53539**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|python-multipart|0.0.30|[CVE-2026-53539](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53539)|\n\nPython-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Prior to 0.0.30, when parsing application/x-www-form-urlencoded bodies, QuerystringParser located the field separator with a two step lookup: it first scanned the entire remaining buffer for \u0026, and only when no \u0026 existed anywhere ahead did it fall back to scanning for ;. For a body that uses ; as the separator and contains no \u0026, every field iteration performed a full failed \u0026 scan over the entire remaining buffer before locating the nearby ;. With N semicolon separated fields in a chunk of size B, this yields O(B^2) byte comparisons per chunk. An attacker can submit a small crafted body of the form a;a;a;... and cause the parser to spend seconds of CPU per request. A handful of concurrent requests can exhaust worker processes. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.0.30."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-40347",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "python-multipart: Python-Multipart: Denial of Service via crafted multipart/form-data requests"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Python-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Versions prior to 0.0.26 have a denial of service vulnerability when parsing crafted `multipart/form-data` requests with large preamble or epilogue sections. Upgrade to version 0.0.26 or later, which skips ahead to the next boundary candidate when processing leading CR/LF data and immediately discards epilogue data after the closing boundary."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-40347",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-40347\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: python-multipart\nFixed Version: 0.0.26\nLink: [CVE-2026-40347](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-40347)\nPython-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Versions prior to 0.0.26 have a denial of service vulnerability when parsing crafted `multipart/form-data` requests with large preamble or epilogue sections. Upgrade to version 0.0.26 or later, which skips ahead to the next boundary candidate when processing leading CR/LF data and immediately discards epilogue data after the closing boundary.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-40347**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|python-multipart|0.0.26|[CVE-2026-40347](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-40347)|\n\nPython-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Versions prior to 0.0.26 have a denial of service vulnerability when parsing crafted `multipart/form-data` requests with large preamble or epilogue sections. Upgrade to version 0.0.26 or later, which skips ahead to the next boundary candidate when processing leading CR/LF data and immediately discards epilogue data after the closing boundary."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.3,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53537",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "multipart: Python-Multipart: Information disclosure via header parsing discrepancy"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Python-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Prior to 0.0.30, parse_options_header parsed Content-Disposition (and Content-Type) headers with email.message.Message, which transparently applies RFC 2231/5987 decoding. The extended parameter syntax (filename*=charset'lang'value, name*=..., and the filename*0/filename*1 continuation form) is decoded and surfaced under the bare filename/name key, and overrides the plain parameter when both are present. RFC 7578 §4.2 explicitly forbids the filename* form in multipart/form-data. Components that follow RFC 7578, or that do not implement RFC 2231/5987 decoding for multipart/form-data (WAFs, proxies, gateways), may interpret such a header differently. An attacker can exploit that difference to smuggle a different field name or filename past an upstream inspector to the backend. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.0.30."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53537",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53537\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: python-multipart\nFixed Version: 0.0.30\nLink: [CVE-2026-53537](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53537)\nPython-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Prior to 0.0.30, parse_options_header parsed Content-Disposition (and Content-Type) headers with email.message.Message, which transparently applies RFC 2231/5987 decoding. The extended parameter syntax (filename*=charset'lang'value, name*=..., and the filename*0/filename*1 continuation form) is decoded and surfaced under the bare filename/name key, and overrides the plain parameter when both are present. RFC 7578 §4.2 explicitly forbids the filename* form in multipart/form-data. Components that follow RFC 7578, or that do not implement RFC 2231/5987 decoding for multipart/form-data (WAFs, proxies, gateways), may interpret such a header differently. An attacker can exploit that difference to smuggle a different field name or filename past an upstream inspector to the backend. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.0.30.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53537**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|python-multipart|0.0.30|[CVE-2026-53537](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53537)|\n\nPython-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Prior to 0.0.30, parse_options_header parsed Content-Disposition (and Content-Type) headers with email.message.Message, which transparently applies RFC 2231/5987 decoding. The extended parameter syntax (filename*=charset'lang'value, name*=..., and the filename*0/filename*1 continuation form) is decoded and surfaced under the bare filename/name key, and overrides the plain parameter when both are present. RFC 7578 §4.2 explicitly forbids the filename* form in multipart/form-data. Components that follow RFC 7578, or that do not implement RFC 2231/5987 decoding for multipart/form-data (WAFs, proxies, gateways), may interpret such a header differently. An attacker can exploit that difference to smuggle a different field name or filename past an upstream inspector to the backend. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.0.30."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 3.7,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "3.7",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53538",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "python-multipart: Python-Multipart: Information disclosure due to parser differential in form data handling"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Python-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Prior to 0.0.30, QuerystringParser treated ; as a field separator in application/x-www-form-urlencoded bodies, in addition to \u0026. The WHATWG URL standard, modern browsers, and Python's urllib.parse (since the CVE-2021-23336 fix) treat only \u0026 as a separator. This creates a parser differential: the same bytes are tokenized into different fields than a WHATWG compliant intermediary would produce, allowing an attacker to smuggle extra form fields past an upstream body inspecting component. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.0.30."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53538",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53538\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: python-multipart\nFixed Version: 0.0.30\nLink: [CVE-2026-53538](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53538)\nPython-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Prior to 0.0.30, QuerystringParser treated ; as a field separator in application/x-www-form-urlencoded bodies, in addition to \u0026. The WHATWG URL standard, modern browsers, and Python's urllib.parse (since the CVE-2021-23336 fix) treat only \u0026 as a separator. This creates a parser differential: the same bytes are tokenized into different fields than a WHATWG compliant intermediary would produce, allowing an attacker to smuggle extra form fields past an upstream body inspecting component. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.0.30.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53538**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|python-multipart|0.0.30|[CVE-2026-53538](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53538)|\n\nPython-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Prior to 0.0.30, QuerystringParser treated ; as a field separator in application/x-www-form-urlencoded bodies, in addition to \u0026. The WHATWG URL standard, modern browsers, and Python's urllib.parse (since the CVE-2021-23336 fix) treat only \u0026 as a separator. This creates a parser differential: the same bytes are tokenized into different fields than a WHATWG compliant intermediary would produce, allowing an attacker to smuggle extra form fields past an upstream body inspecting component. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.0.30."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 3.7,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "3.7",
                "tags": [
